{"headword":"סָבִיב","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>subst.</strong>, used mostly as <strong>adv.</strong> and <strong>prep.</strong>, <strong>circuit, round about</strong>:—cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">סְבִיב</span> †<a data-ref=\"Amos 3:11\" href=\"/Amos.3.11\">Am 3:11</a>; pl. cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">סְבִיבֵי</span> †<a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 32:44\" href=\"/Jeremiah.32.44\">Je 32:44</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 33:13\" href=\"/Jeremiah.33.13\">33:13</a>, sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">סְבִיבֶיךָ</span> etc. (10 times), much oftener <span dir=\"rtl\">סְבִיבוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 7:24\" href=\"/Exodus.7.24\">Ex 7:24</a> + 22 times, <span dir=\"rtl\">סְבִיבוֹתַי</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">תֶיךָ</span>-, etc., <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 17:14\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.17.14\">Dt 17:14</a>, etc. (48 times):—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"in sg.:—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"as <strong>subst.</strong> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:8\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.8\">1 Ch 11:8</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מן־המלוא וְעַד־הַסָּבִיב</span> and to <em>the parts round about</em>."}],"num":"a."},{"senses":[{"definition":"as <strong>adv.acc.</strong> <span dir=\"rtl\">סָבִיב</span> (in) <em>a circuit</em>, i.e. <em>round about</em>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 23:17\" href=\"/Genesis.23.17\">Gn 23:17</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּכָל־גְּבֻלוֹ סָבִיב</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 19:12\" href=\"/Exodus.19.12\">Ex 19:12</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 25:11\" href=\"/Exodus.25.11\">25:11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 25:24\" href=\"/Exodus.25.24\">24</a>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 25:25\" href=\"/Exodus.25.25\">25</a>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 1:5\" href=\"/Leviticus.1.5\">Lv 1:5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 1:11\" href=\"/Leviticus.1.11\">11</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל הַמִּזְבֵּחַ סָבִיב</span>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 20:29\" href=\"/Judges.20.29\">Ju 20:29</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 3:1\" href=\"/I_Kings.3.1\">1 K 3:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 5:11\" href=\"/I_Kings.5.11\">5:11</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 3:7\" href=\"/Psalms.3.7\">ψ 3:7</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲשֶׁר ס׳ שָׁתוּ עָלָ֑י</span>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 12:9\" href=\"/Psalms.12.9\">12:9</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 34:8\" href=\"/Psalms.34.8\">34:8</a> + often; sometimes doubled, for the sake of emphasis, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 4:3\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.4.3\">2 Ch 4:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 8:10\" href=\"/Ezekiel.8.10\">Ez 8:10</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל הַקִּיר ס׳ ס׳</span>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 37:2\" href=\"/Psalms.37.2\">37:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 40:5\" href=\"/Psalms.40.5\">40:5</a> and often in <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 40-43\" href=\"/Ezekiel.40-43\">Ez 40–43</a>."}],"num":"b."},{"senses":[{"definition":"as <strong>prep.:</strong> (<em>a</em>) †<a data-ref=\"Amos 3:11\" href=\"/Amos.3.11\">Am 3:11</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">צַר וּסְבִיב הָאָרֶץ</span> <em>distress</em>, and that <em>in the circuit of</em> (= <em>round about</em>) the land (but read prob. with 𝔖 <span dir=\"rtl\">יְסֹבֵב</span> <em>will encircle</em>). (<em>b</em>) <span dir=\"rtl\">סָבִיב לְ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:13\" href=\"/Exodus.16.13\">Ex 16:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 40:33\" href=\"/Exodus.40.33\">40:33</a> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 1:50\" href=\"/Numbers.1.50\">Nu 1:50</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 1:53\" href=\"/Numbers.1.53\">53</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 2:2\" href=\"/Numbers.2.2\">2:2</a> <a data-ref=\"Judges 7:21\" href=\"/Judges.7.21\">Ju 7:21</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 6:5\" href=\"/I_Kings.6.5\">1 K 6:5</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 18:32\" href=\"/I_Kings.18.32\">18:32</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 18:35\" href=\"/I_Kings.18.35\">35</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 41:10\" href=\"/Ezekiel.41.10\">Ez 41:10</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 41:16\" href=\"/Ezekiel.41.16\">16</a> <a data-ref=\"Job 19:12\" href=\"/Job.19.12\">Jb 19:12</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 34:8\" href=\"/Psalms.34.8\">ψ 34:8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 78:28\" href=\"/Psalms.78.28\">78:28</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 125:2\" href=\"/Psalms.125.2\">125:2</a><sup>(×2)</sup> <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳ סָבִיב לְעַמּוֹ</span>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 128:3\" href=\"/Psalms.128.3\">128:3</a> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 3:7\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.3.7\">Ct 3:7</a> <a data-ref=\"Nahum 3:8\" href=\"/Nahum.3.8\">Na 3:8</a>. (<em>c</em>) strangely, <span dir=\"rtl\">סָבִיב אֵת</span> †<a data-ref=\"I Kings 6:5\" href=\"/I_Kings.6.5\">1 K 6:5</a> (om.𝔊), <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 43:17\" href=\"/Ezekiel.43.17\">Ez 43:17</a>."}],"num":"c."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">מִסָּבִיב</span><sub>42</sub>, <em>from round about, from every side</em>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:33\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.33\">Ez 16:33</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:37\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.37\">37</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:22\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.22\">23:22</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 37:21\" href=\"/Ezekiel.37.21\">37:21</a>, but usually (<span dir=\"rtl\">מִן</span> <strong>1 c</strong>) = <em>on every side</em>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 4:17\" href=\"/Jeremiah.4.17\">Je 4:17</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">הָיוּ עָלֶיהָ מִסָּבִיב</span>, <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 42:25\" href=\"/Isaiah.42.25\">Is 42:25</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">וַתְּלַהֲטֵהוּ מ׳</span>, <a data-ref=\"Joel 4:11\" href=\"/Joel.4.11\">Jo 4:11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joel 4:12\" href=\"/Joel.4.12\">12</a>; †<span dir=\"rtl\">מָגוֹר מִסָּבִיב</span> terror <em>on every side!</em> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 6:25\" href=\"/Jeremiah.6.25\">Je 6:25</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 20:3\" href=\"/Jeremiah.20.3\">20:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 20:10\" href=\"/Jeremiah.20.10\">10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 46:5\" href=\"/Jeremiah.46.5\">46:5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 49:29\" href=\"/Jeremiah.49.29\">49:29</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 31:14\" href=\"/Psalms.31.14\">ψ 31:14</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 2:22\" href=\"/Lamentations.2.22\">La 2:22</a>; especially in the Deut. phrases <span dir=\"rtl\">אוֹיְבִים מ׳</span>, or <span dir=\"rtl\">הֵנִיחַ מ׳</span> (sometimes in combin.), as <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 12:10\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.12.10\">Dt 12:10</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">והניח לכם מכל־אויביכם מ׳</span>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 25:19\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.25.19\">25:19</a> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 21:42\" href=\"/Joshua.21.42\">Jos 21:42</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיָּנַח י׳ לָהֶם מ׳</span>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 23:1\" href=\"/Joshua.23.1\">23:1</a> <a data-ref=\"Judges 2:14\" href=\"/Judges.2.14\">Ju 2:14</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 8:34\" href=\"/Judges.8.34\">8:34</a> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 12:11\" href=\"/I_Samuel.12.11\">1 S 12:11</a> +; <span dir=\"rtl\">מִסָּבִיב לְ</span> <em>from round about</em>, †<a data-ref=\"Numbers 16:24\" href=\"/Numbers.16.24\">Nu 16:24</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 16:27\" href=\"/Numbers.16.27\">27</a>.—On <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:21\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.21\">1 S 14:21</a> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 24:6\" href=\"/II_Samuel.24.6\">2 S 24:6</a> <a data-ref=\"Job 10:8\" href=\"/Job.10.8\">Jb 10:8</a> v. <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, סָבַב\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_סָבַב\">סָבַב</a>."}],"num":"d."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"In <em>plur.:</em>—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"†<span dir=\"rtl\">סְבִיבִים</span>: (<em>a</em>) in masc. sense, <em>those round about</em>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 76:12\" href=\"/Psalms.76.12\">ψ 76:12</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">כָּל־סְבִיבָיו יֹבִילוּשַׁי</span>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 89:8\" href=\"/Psalms.89.8\">89:8</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 48:17\" href=\"/Jeremiah.48.17\">Je 48:17</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 48:39\" href=\"/Jeremiah.48.39\">39</a>. (<em>b</em>) in neuter sense, <em>the parts round about</em>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 49:5\" href=\"/Jeremiah.49.5\">Je 49:5</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מִכָּל־סְבִיבָ֑יִךְ</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">בִּסְבִיבֵי ירושׁלם</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 32:44\" href=\"/Jeremiah.32.44\">32:44</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 33:13\" href=\"/Jeremiah.33.13\">33:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 21:14\" href=\"/Jeremiah.21.14\">21:14</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">וְאָֽכְלָה כָּל־סְבִיבֶיהָ</span>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 46:14\" href=\"/Jeremiah.46.14\">46:14</a>; with the force of a <strong>prep.</strong>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 50:3\" href=\"/Psalms.50.3\">ψ 50:3</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">וסביביו נשׂערה מאד</span>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 97:2\" href=\"/Psalms.97.2\">97:2</a> <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 1:17\" href=\"/Lamentations.1.17\">La 1:17</a>."}],"num":"a."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">סְבִיבוֹת</span>: (<em>a</em>) as <strong>subst.</strong> (α) <em>circuits</em>, <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 1:6\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.1.6\">Ec 1:6</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ועל סביבותיו שָׁב הָרוּחַ</span>; (β) <em>the parts round about</em>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 22:4\" href=\"/Numbers.22.4\">Nu 22:4</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ילחכו הקהל את־כל־סְבִיבֹתֵינוּ</span>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 17:26\" href=\"/Jeremiah.17.26\">Je 17:26</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 50:32\" href=\"/Jeremiah.50.32\">50:32</a> (cf. <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 21:14\" href=\"/Jeremiah.21.14\">21:14</a> supr.); with ref. to their inhabitants, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 44:19\" href=\"/Psalms.44.19\">ψ 44:19</a> = <a data-ref=\"Psalms 79:4\" href=\"/Psalms.79.4\">79:4</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">לעג וקלם לסב׳</span>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:57\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.57\">Ez 16:57</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 28:24\" href=\"/Ezekiel.28.24\">28:24</a> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 9:16\" href=\"/Daniel.9.16\">Dn 9:16</a>. (<em>b</em>) with the force of a <strong>prep.</strong> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 7:24\" href=\"/Exodus.7.24\">Ex 7:24</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">סְבִיבֹת הַיְאֹר</span> lit. (in) <em>the circuits of</em> the Nile = <em>round about</em> the Nile, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 11:24\" href=\"/Numbers.11.24\">Nu 11:24</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 11:31\" href=\"/Numbers.11.31\">31</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 11:32\" href=\"/Numbers.11.32\">32</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 35:2\" href=\"/Numbers.35.2\">35:2</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">סְבִיבֹתֵיהֶם</span>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 7:18\" href=\"/Judges.7.18\">Ju 7:18</a> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 26:5\" href=\"/I_Samuel.26.5\">1 S 26:5</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 26:7\" href=\"/I_Samuel.26.7\">7</a> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 6:17\" href=\"/II_Kings.6.17\">2 K 6:17</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">סביבֹת אלישׁע</span>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 18:12\" href=\"/Psalms.18.12\">ψ 18:12</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 27:6\" href=\"/Psalms.27.6\">27:6</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">על אֹיְבַי סביבותי</span>, etc.; often idiom. preceded by <span dir=\"rtl\">אשׁר</span>, as <a data-ref=\"Genesis 35:5\" href=\"/Genesis.35.5\">Gn 35:5</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">הערים אשׁר סביבותיהם</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 41:48\" href=\"/Genesis.41.48\">41:48</a> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 25:44\" href=\"/Leviticus.25.44\">Lv 25:44</a> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 16:34\" href=\"/Numbers.16.34\">Nu 16:34</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 6:14\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.6.14\">Dt 6:14</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 13:8\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.13.8\">13:8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 17:14\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.17.14\">17:14</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 21:2\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.21.2\">21:2</a> +. In the same sense <span dir=\"rtl\">מִסְּבִיבוֹתָם</span> + <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 28:26\" href=\"/Ezekiel.28.26\">Ez 28:26</a>."}],"num":"b."}],"num":"2."}]},"rid":"BDB06628","strong_numbers":["5439"],"next_hw":"מֵסַב²","prev_hw":"סִבָּה","occurrences":"336","quotes":[],"GK":["4585","6017"],"TWOT":["1456b"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}